//0.9.10 v2.4 canary: consumer module. Imports lib and invokes the
//INSTANCE overload of Mix.f() through the imported free function
//callF (the 0.9.11 O2 idiom — the external-stub path does not support
//calling an imported class's instance method directly). Expected exit
//code 42.
//
//Why 42 (kept <= 255 on purpose): the process exit code is the full
//32-bit return value of main(), but bash/POSIX `$?` truncates it to
//its low 8 bits (999 mod 256 == 231 is the shape this test guards
//against). Pinning the expected value below 256 keeps the assertion
//unambiguous under any shell — see memory nlang-exit-code-limit.
//A staticness linkage bug would resolve the import to the decoy static
//f(int x) and yield a different value, so 42 vs (x*1001) is decisive.
import lib;

int main() {
	lib.Mix m = lib.Mix();
	return lib.callF(m);
}
